From 5ba6eeb374f1c2d4069b45bc5b117955bebdef99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 22:27:18 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] demux: expose how a video maps a sphere as
 track-list/N/demux-projection

A 360 or VR180 video says in its container how the sphere is laid out
in the frame (MP4 sv3d, Matroska Projection), and FFmpeg exports it as
spherical side data, but mpv did not pass it on, so a player could not
tell such a video from an ordinary one without parsing the file itself.

Read the spherical side data of the stream in demux_lavf and
ProjectionType in demux_mkv, and expose the result in the track list:
equirectangular, half-equirectangular (the front half, as VR180 writes
it: an equirectangular picture with half of the width cut off), the
other equirectangular tiles, cubemap and mesh. Nothing changes for
playback; a script or a libmpv client can now choose a v360 filter.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
